preparation_steps:
- step_number: 1
  action: DISSOLVE
  description: 1. Dissolve ingredients (except sulfur, carbonate, vitamins, growth-stimulating
    factors and Na-dithionite), boil medium for 1 min, then cool to room temperature
    under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere.
- step_number: 2
  action: ADJUST_PH
  description: Adjust pH to 6.0 and dispense under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere
    into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials which contain already the appropriate
    amount of sulfur, only to 30% of their volume to allow for a large head space.
- step_number: 3
  action: AUTOCLAVE
  description: Autoclave at a temperature of 110°C for 20 min! Add vitamins, growth-stimulating
    factors from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas and carbonate
    and Na-dithionite from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 80% N2 and
    20% CO2 gas atmosphere.
- step_number: 4
  action: FILTER_STERILIZE
  description: Vitamins and dithionite are sterilized by filtration. Adjust pH of
    the complete medium to 6.0, if necessary.
- step_number: 5
  action: MIX
  description: 2. After inoculation use 1 bar overpressure of sterile 80% H2 and 20%
    CO2 gas mixture.
ph_value: 6.0
